---
import Tunnel from '../../../layouts/Tunnel.astro';
import Choice from '../../../components/Choice.astro';
// DRAFT
---
<Tunnel title="Drive Health Test | Save My Gig" status="Full_Recovery" risk>
  <div class="review-flag">DRAFT, review pending.</div>
  <div class="step-label">Step 2</div>
  <h2 style="margin-bottom:1rem">Test the drive with a FULL format</h2>

  <p class="dim">A full format works the whole drive, not just the index. Stress test and clean slate in one.</p>

  <!-- The rescue-route DJ copied their files two screens ago; the "I can
       replace it" DJ copied nothing. This screen wipes the drive for BOTH, so
       it says so itself instead of relying on a pad description upstream. -->
  <div class="alert-card" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem">
    <div style="font-size:20px" aria-hidden="true">⚠️</div>
    <div>
      <strong>This wipes everything still on the drive.</strong> Only what you
      already copied off survives. If anything on it is irreplaceable and not
      yet copied, stop and go back.
    </div>
  </div>

  <ul class="checklist">
    <li>Format the USB: <span class="mono" translate="no">FAT32</span> · <span class="mono" translate="no">MBR</span> · <strong>uncheck Quick Format</strong>.</li>
    <li>A full pass on a big stick takes time. That is the test working.</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="question">Did the full format complete with no errors?</p>

  <Choice step="fr_health"
    a={{ href: '/protocol/full-recovery/rebuild', label: 'YES - CLEAN FORMAT' }}
    b={{ href: '/protocol/full-recovery/retire', label: 'NO - ERRORS OR CRAWLING', desc: 'The hardware is failing. It never gets trusted with a gig again.' }}
  />
</Tunnel>
